.TH SMCTL 1 "2026-10-29" "smctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
smctl \- control your Mac's System Management Controller from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smctl
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smctl
is a CLI-first tool for controlling hardware that macOS normally manages on
its own \(em fan speed, battery charging, external display power, and power
telemetry \(em on Apple Silicon Macs.
.PP
Reading sensors works without privileges. Battery and fan control are applied
by a root LaunchDaemon,
.BR smctld ,
which the CLI talks to over XPC. Install it once with
.BR "sudo smctl daemon install" .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS sensors
.B smctl sensors
.RB [ --watch ]
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
Print temperatures (grouped by sensor), fan RPM and mode, battery, and package
power.
.B --watch
refreshes every second until interrupted;
.B --json
emits machine-readable output. Needs no daemon and no root.
.RE
.SS battery
.B smctl battery status
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
Charge level, charging state, time estimate, and the configured limit.
.RE
.B smctl battery maintain
.IR LIMIT
.RB [ --force-discharge ]
.RS
Keep the charge within a limit. LIMIT is a single percent
.RI ( 80 ),
a range
.RI ( 70-80 ),
or
.BR stop .
A dead-band prevents charge/discharge flapping near the threshold.
.B --force-discharge
actively drains down to the band by cutting adapter power while above the
upper bound.
.RE
.B smctl battery charge
.IR PERCENT
.RS
One-shot charge up to PERCENT, then stop.
.RE
.B smctl battery discharge
.IR PERCENT
.RS
Cut adapter power and discharge down to PERCENT. Runs in the foreground;
the daemon restores adapter power on completion, client disconnect, or renewal
timeout. Failed restoration is retried.
.RE
.B smctl battery charging
.RI ( on | off )
.RS
Manually allow or block battery charging. An active maintain policy may
override this on its next evaluation.
.RE
.B smctl battery adapter
.RI ( on | off )
.RS
Manually enable or cut adapter power input.
.RE
.SS fan
.B smctl fan status
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
Per-fan actual, target, minimum, and maximum RPM, plus the control mode.
.RE
.B smctl fan set
.IR RPM
.RB [ --fan
.IR N ]
.RB [ --force ]
.RS
Set a manual fan target in RPM, clamped to the fan's reported min/max. The
applied target is printed, so a clamp is visible.
.B --fan
targets one fan (0-based); omit it to set all fans.
.B --force
permits targets below the minimum, but only when
.B allow_below_minimum
is set under
.B [safety]
in the config; the maximum is always a hard ceiling.
.RE
.B smctl fan auto
.RB [ --fan
.IR N ]
.RS
Return fans to system control. While a curve profile is active, restoring a
single fan is rejected because the curve re-asserts control every second; run
.B smctl fan profile auto
first.
.RE
.B smctl fan profile
.IR NAME
.RS
Apply a fan profile:
.BR auto ,
.BR quiet ,
.BR full ,
or a custom curve defined in the config.
.RE
.SS power
.B smctl power
.RB [ status ]
.RB [ --watch ]
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
Thermal pressure, CPU throttling (percent of full clock), and package, system,
and input power. Needs no daemon and no root.
.RE
.SS display
.B smctl display list
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
List external DDC/CI-capable displays. The built-in panel is not listed.
.RE
.B smctl display brightness
.RB [ PERCENT ]
.RB [ --display
.IR INDEX|UUID ]
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
Read or set brightness as a percentage. The percentage is scaled to the
display's own luminance range.
.RE
.B smctl display power
.RB [ ( on | off ) ]
.RB [ --display
.IR INDEX|UUID ]
.RS
Read or set display power over DDC. The display stays in the macOS layout
while soft-off.
.RE
.SS alert
.B smctl alert list
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
Show configured rules, validity, and redacted action targets. Webhook query
strings and exec arguments are deliberately hidden.
.RE
.B smctl alert status
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
Per-rule state
.RI ( armed | pending | cooling | firing )
and recent events.
.RE
.B smctl alert test
.IR NAME
.RS
Fire a rule's action immediately to verify the webhook or command. Requires
root or an admin user.
.RE
.SS daemon
.B smctl daemon
.RB ( install | uninstall | restart | reload | status | capabilities | ping | logs )
.RS
Manage
.BR smctld .
.B install/uninstall
require root.
.B install
updates the root-owned helper in /Library/PrivilegedHelperTools and restarts
the service. Run it after every
.BR "brew upgrade" .
.B uninstall
restores system control of fans and charging before removing the daemon.
.B restart
restarts the installed copy and reloads configuration; it does not copy a new
binary.
.B reload
re-reads /etc/smctl/config.toml without restarting; requires root or an admin
user.
.B status
shows the config path, evaluation period, and last error.
.B capabilities
shows detected fan, charging, and adapter control support.
.B logs
wraps
.BR "log show"
for the smctl subsystem and accepts
.BR --last " (e.g. 10m, 1h, 2d)."
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Policy lives in
.IR /etc/smctl/config.toml .
The file is root-owned and mode 0600 because alert action targets can contain
secrets. CLI commands update the keys they own in place: comments, unknown
keys, and the
.B [[fan.curves]]
and
.B [[alert]]
tables written by hand are preserved. A symlinked config is updated through
the link. After hand-editing, run
.BR "sudo smctl daemon reload" .
.PP
.B [battery]
.RS
.BR limit " (\(dq80\(dq, 70-80, or \(dq100\(dq),"
.BR sleep_policy " (strict | relaxed),"
.BR force_discharge " (bool)."
.RE
.B [fan]
.RS
.B profile
(named profile or custom curve). Custom curves are declared as
.B [[fan.curves]]
tables with
.BR name ,
.BR sensors ,
.BR points " ([[temperature, rpm-or-\(dqmax\(dq]], …),"
.BR hysteresis ,
.BR slew_rate ,
.BR fall_slew_rate ,
and optional
.BR weights .
.RE
.B [safety]
.RS
.BR temp_ceiling " (default 100C, hard-capped at 105C),"
.BR allow_below_minimum " (bool)."
The thermal guard cannot be disabled.
.RE
.B [update]
.RS
.B check
enables the once-a-day GitHub release check.
.RE
.B [sentry]
.RS
.BR dsn " (empty disables Sentry),"
.BR environment ,
.BR debug ,
.BR traces_sample_rate .
.RE
.B [[alert]]
.RS
Rules with
.BR name ,
.BR on " (temp | guard | write-error),"
.BR sensor ,
.BR above ,
.BR for ,
.BR cooldown ,
.BR resolve ,
.B action " (webhook | exec | log),"
.BR url ,
.B command.
Exec actions run as root; commands use argv arrays and never a shell.
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/smctl/config.toml
Declarative policy configuration, root-owned, mode 0600.
.TP
.I /Library/LaunchDaemons/one.leaper.smctl.daemon.plist
The installed LaunchDaemon.
.TP
.I /Library/PrivilegedHelperTools/one.leaper.smctl.daemon
The protected copy of the daemon executed by launchd.
.SH PRIVACY
The CLI itself does not make network requests. The daemon can make outbound
requests for the daily GitHub releases update check, user-configured alert
webhooks, and optional Sentry crash/error reporting when
.B [sentry]
.B dsn
is configured. Disable the update check with
.B check = false
under
.BR [update] ,
leave
.B [sentry] dsn
empty, and configure no webhook alerts for a fully offline daemon.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B smctl
exits 0 on success and non-zero on error (64 for usage and validation errors).
.SH SEE ALSO
Project home and full documentation: https://github.com/leaperone/smctl
